lines+=['','Actual forwarding attack exposure depends on whether the configured relay carries transit traffic. A case with zero malicious drops is not evidence of forwarding-attack protection; it remains a valid host-misuse test. No such case is excluded from the tables.\n\nOnset delay is root alarm global time minus the first actual ORACLE_HOST execution time. Oracle events are used only by this independent evaluation, never by the gateway. Sparse alarm coverage counts an alarm during execution or within15source-seconds of a burst’s last execution; an existing alarm counts as coverage, not a new detection. Source-clock nominal delays, pre-attack target warnings, warnings within15seconds before actual execution, and post-attack tails are also retained in runs.json. A near-zero delay for a policy already warning before the attack must not be interpreted as fast discrimination of that attack.','', '## What was integrated','','- All ten simulated nodes use actual instruction-emulated Z1 firmware, including the radio root. Arithmetic workloads, RPL traffic, packet dropping, resource counters, signatures, queries, grants, source redirection and helper forwarding execute.','- A host gateway ports the earlier source-work/receipt/lease controller and runs the workload-aware host predictor, GRU and classifier. Host warnings raise query priority and exclude suspected helpers. Host evidence alone does not disconnect a device.','- Root verifies HMAC/session/sequence on host reports; authenticates network messages; gateway validates network report freshness, nonce, count and action scope. Source-work reports retain original/repair/redirect counts and lease identities.','- Decisions reserve at most480B per10-second decision, with mandatory reporting counted separately. Actual command sequence, authenticated payload, helper forwarding and offer/receipt conservation are independently audited.','- Root commands are queued and transmitted at125ms polling intervals. Inference/bridge wall time is outside simulation time; this is not a real-time deployment qualification.','', '## Models, supervision and protocol','','Source1111/1112 uses complete benign runs for resource prediction and AE fitting;1113/1114 is benign-only calibration. Final1151/bypass/target2 and1152/grid/target3 were excluded until freezing. Each has benign authorized mixed activity/loss;250-round hidden CPU plus selective forwarding; and1,000-round4s/60s CPU bursts plus legitimate mixed traffic, selective forwarding and0.85nominal reception. Each run lasts900s, application offers180–840s, configured attacks400–700s and root-authorized work300–780s.','', 'The combined model retains pretrained supervised GRU/classifier weights; its resource predictor and benign thresholds are recalibrated on this rig. CIPHER-style uses correlation-grouped LSTMs(width2), reconstruction over18available fields, window16,250epochs,Adam0.05,batch32. CONTRAST-style uses CPU/TX LSTM(width8), window32,200epochs,Adam0.001,batch256. Both fit benign-only new sources and use three-of-five thresholds above complete benign calibration maxima. The original CIPHER/CONTRAST distributed frameworks, original full feature schemas and original long-duration conditions are not reproduced by this compact panel. Their adaptations are inserted into exactly the same gateway controller. Baseline implementation scope: ../baselines/README.md.','', 'The comparison therefore measures these implemented adaptations at the declared settings. Different supervision and feature access prevent a claim that an original benign-only published framework is generally inferior. Source-only minmax/benign predictor fitting, development-only calibration, fixed final settings and whole deployment splits avoid row/window leakage.','', 'Gateway source provenance: the model hash/timestamp was recorded before final runs. Firmware source/binary hashes are checked per run. The gateway source hash was recorded after completion; independent saved-model replay reproduced recorded actions. A pre-run gateway-source hash was not recorded by the accepted training process.', '', '## Paper claim boundaries','','The implemented research direction is joint accounting for authorized workload and authorized defensive actions before spending evidence/repair resources. Whether it improves the complete trade-off is determined by the paired table, including any cost increase or service loss. A successful integration is a deliverable; it does not by itself establish a new algorithm or literature-wide novelty.','', '- Only two deployment blocks and one seed per topology are used. Seed and topology are confounded. This is a compact varied study, not a robustness or significance certificate.','- Honest isolated resource measurement and benign startup calibration remain assumptions. No TEE/attestation, compromised-root tolerance or full-host-forgery protection is implemented.','- Host alarms do not stop unauthorized CPU execution. The implemented response investigates evidence and repairs delivery; it is not host-process containment.', '- Optional task-integrity/fallback is not included in this study. FIT hardware testing remains deferred.','- Mandatory host-telemetry cost is charged to every policy. Separate deployment ablation would be needed to measure removal of that instrumentation itself.','- The protocol bounds admitted defense payload, not physical energy, retransmissions or all network load. Keys are laboratory fixtures, not a deployed key-management system.','- Original network-priority weights were fitted on the earlier native rig and remain frozen. Transfer limits are part of the test.','', '## Reproducible outputs','','- results/paper-summary.csv and paper-runs.csv: full comparison and case-level tables.','- results/comparison-table.tex: LaTeX table.','- results/paired-differences.json: all matched differences.','- results/runs.json: detection, recovery, service, costs, genuine-work accounting, helper and command counts.','- results/figures/: exportable PNG/PDF figures.','- results/training-freeze.json and models/combined.pkl: frozen artifact and source/calibration settings.','- configs/final.json, scenarios/, logs/: exact fresh runs and raw evidence.','- results/validation.json and manifest.json: final verification and hashes.']
